<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Beacon digest fires. Install + load with:
       cp deploy/com.beacon.digest.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
       launchctl bootout  gui/$UID/com.beacon.digest 2>/dev/null
       launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.beacon.digest.plist

     Three fires a day — 08:00, 12:00 and 16:30 local time (Asia/Jakarta on this box; launchd
     reads the system zone, which is also config.LOCAL_TZ). Each fire polls the sources and
     pushes the Telegram digest, then exits: no RunAtLoad, no KeepAlive, nothing to kill.
     deploy/hourly-digest.sh holds the lock and watchdog that cap a run.

     Why three and not eight: a full poll of ~59 pollable seeds at 1 rps runs 30-45 min, so the
     old :30-past-every-hour window spent most of the day polling and the lock did real work
     skipping collisions (changed 2026-09-11). The gaps here are 4h/4.5h against a 50 min
     watchdog, so a fire can never meet the next one. Nothing is lost to a skipped or killed
     run either way: application/notify.py writes seen_matches only AFTER the notifier
     succeeds, so unnotified matches roll into the next digest.

     08:00 is the fire most likely to land late. A LaunchAgent lives in the user's GUI domain,
     so it only fires while logged in, and a sleeping Mac is not woken. launchd runs a missed
     fire once on login/wake (they coalesce), so logging in at 08:20 gets the 08:00 fire at
     08:20. `sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 07:59:00` if it must be guaranteed.

     TCC: keep the checkout OUT of ~/Documents, ~/Desktop and ~/Downloads. A launchd-started
     job has no access there and dies before it starts — `Operation not permitted`, exit 126
     (proved 2026-09-10; hand-runs still work, because the terminal holds the grant). The move
     to ~/Projects/beacon is confirmed good: the 2026-09-11 09:30 fire ran the script.

     Paths are absolute because launchd has no working shell. Telegram creds are read from
     app_settings in beacon.db (Settings UI) and every path in Settings resolves from the repo
     root, so no BEACON_* env is needed here. Moving the checkout means editing this file.
     Tail logs at /tmp/beacon.digest.{out,err}.log. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.beacon.digest</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>/Users/tomtomtomtom/Projects/beacon/deploy/hourly-digest.sh</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/tomtomtomtom/Projects/beacon</string>
    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <array>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>8</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>12</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>0</integer></dict>
        <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>16</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    </array>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/beacon.digest.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/beacon.digest.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
